● Signal is taken from the microphone and noise is added to it through the AWGN channel.
● A random white noise of 0 mean, is generated from another block.
● The second random noise is adapted to the original signal+noise made.
● FDAF block is used to perform the adaptive filtering.
● Output of the block will be adapted to the only co-related part, which is white noise.
● Output of the FDAF block is hence the adapted noise.
● Input signal is subtracted from FDAF output and the final output is taken.

Expectations and Explanations(Noise Masking with Adaptive Noise Shaping) :
● The output is not very effectively filtering out the noise, but the noise which is even
coming after the process is not the white noise, which is the original one put in. Hence, it
can be said that the original AWGN white noise is removed. There are some distortions,
which could be due to the communication channel and also acts as a shaped noise to
output. Also the snr display, verifies this claim. Hence, it can be said with reasonable
confidence that the objectives were fulfilled.

● LMS block was not used since it did not remove white noise from the system, even
though its output is much clearer than FDAF block output. The purpose of removing
white noise is fulfilled by the FDAF block.
